{"id":141171826477883,"type":"album","name":"After Hours","artist":"The Weeknd","year":2020,"weight":11,"info":{"cover":"https://cdn2.albumoftheyear.org/600x0/album/208717-after-hours-1.jpg","aoty":79,"aoty_user":82,"yt":"Egb1nB18Ojg","links":{"rateyourmusic":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/the-weeknd/after-hours","aoty":"https://www.albumoftheyear.org/album/208717-the-weeknd-after-hours.php"},"desc":"After Hours is the fourth studio album by Canadian singer The Weeknd, released on March 20, 2020, via XO and Republic Records. Thematically, the album explores loneliness, self-loathing and escapism. The standard edition of After Hours has no features, but the remixes edition contains guest appearances from Chromatics and Lil Uzi Vert. The album was supported by four singles: \"Heartless\", \"Blinding Lights\", \"In Your Eyes\" and \"Save Your Tears\". The title track was released as a promotional single. In March 2020, After Hours broke the record for the most global pre-adds in Apple Music history, with over 1.02 million users. ."},"artist_ref":{"id":253154298775734,"name":"The Weeknd","info":{"img":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/The_Weeknd_Portrait_by_Brian_Ziff.jpg?width=500"}},"labels":[],"genres":[{"id":176578125596945,"type":"genre","name":"Contemporary R&B","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":327,"yt":null,"src":"rym"},{"id":57638771788875,"type":"genre","name":"Synthpop","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":260,"yt":null,"src":"rym"},{"id":266557216269112,"type":"genre","name":"Alternative R&B","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":241,"yt":null,"src":"rym"}],"lists":[{"id":6497183387510,"name":"RYM Top — R&B — Alternative R&B","src":"musthear","grp":"rateyourmusic","list_year":null,"rank":15,"year":null,"note":null,"total":200,"scaruffi":null},{"id":184490572271758,"name":"RYM Top — R&B — Contemporary R&B","src":"musthear","grp":"rateyourmusic","list_year":null,"rank":40,"year":null,"note":null,"total":200,"scaruffi":null},{"id":19164